              <flipboard active-id='1' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='To start my visualization, we always need an overview plot to understand all the variables and how they relate to each other in the dataset. It gives the quick view towards our analysis.' captured-sheet='OverView' id='1' />
                  <story-point caption='This plot shows how the height and weight make affect the performance. I sorted height and weight into two categories above average and below average. I didn&apos;t find any strong relationship between them. But by this plot, we can know that the height having the relation with the performance of the player.' captured-sheet='Relation btw Weight and Height' id='2' />
                  <story-point caption='By this plot, we can find and compare the performance of the players according to there hands. It shows that there are a number of good performance players are Right-handed. Still, there are few in left hand having a good performance.' captured-sheet='Relation btw Weight and Height with respect to the Handedness' id='3' />
                  <story-point caption='There are many players in under 72 to 75 with good performance and 180-pound average weight. By using filter we can see there are a number of right-handed players in these criteria of height.' captured-sheet='Avg. Home Run with Height &amp; Weight ' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='This is the overall analysis through which we can find every player&apos;s performance factors. By using the filters and the exploring around in this dashboard we can find every detail physically affect or give an advantage to the payers to perform accordingly.&#10;' captured-sheet='Result Of Final Analysis' id='5'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Avg. Home Run with Height &amp; Weight '>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.0cm6yct0ncco8t141ckgf003l5lm].[Action (Handedness,Name)]'>
